$onText
Generated by nlp2mcp

This file contains the KKT (Karush-Kuhn-Tucker) conditions
for the original NLP model, transformed into MCP format.

KKT System Components:
  - Stationarity: ∇f + J^T λ + J^T ν - π^L + π^U = 0
  - Complementarity: g(x) ⊥ λ, h(x) = 0, bounds ⊥ π
  - Dual feasibility: λ, π^L, π^U ≥ 0
  - Primal feasibility: g(x) ≤ 0, h(x) = 0, lo ≤ x ≤ up
$offText

* ============================================
* Original Model Declarations
* ============================================

Sets
    i /'1', '2', '3', '4', '5', '6'/
;

Alias(i, j);

* ============================================
* Variables (Primal + Multipliers)
* ============================================

* Primal variables: Original decision variables from the NLP
* Multipliers:
*   ν (nu_*): Free multipliers for equality constraints
*   λ (lam_*): Positive multipliers for inequality constraints
*   π^L (piL_*): Positive multipliers for lower bounds
*   π^U (piU_*): Positive multipliers for upper bounds

Variables
    x(i)
    y(i)
    area(i)
    totarea
    nu_areadef(i)
    nu_x_fx_1
    nu_y_fx_1
    nu_y_fx_2
;

Positive Variables
    lam_maxdist(i,j)
;

* ============================================
* NLP Pre-Solve (warm-start for MCP duals)
* ============================================

$onMultiR
$include "data/gamslib/raw/himmel16.gms"
$offMulti

* Transfer NLP duals to MCP multiplier initialization
lam_maxdist.l(i,j) = abs(maxdist.m(i,j));
nu_areadef.l(i) = areadef.m(i);

* Transfer variable marginals to bound multipliers

* Transfer fixed-variable marginals to _fx_ multipliers (#1462)
nu_x_fx_1.l = x.m('1');
nu_y_fx_1.l = y.m('1');
nu_y_fx_2.l = y.m('2');

* Reset any NA/UNDF warm-start multiplier levels to 0 (#1322)
lam_maxdist.l(i,j)$(NOT (lam_maxdist.l(i,j) > -inf and lam_maxdist.l(i,j) < inf)) = 0;
nu_areadef.l(i)$(NOT (nu_areadef.l(i) > -inf and nu_areadef.l(i) < inf)) = 0;
nu_x_fx_1.l$(NOT (nu_x_fx_1.l > -inf and nu_x_fx_1.l < inf)) = 0;
nu_y_fx_1.l$(NOT (nu_y_fx_1.l > -inf and nu_y_fx_1.l < inf)) = 0;
nu_y_fx_2.l$(NOT (nu_y_fx_2.l > -inf and nu_y_fx_2.l < inf)) = 0;

* ============================================
* #1449 (Layer 4): unfix elements fixed by the source $include but
* enforced in the MCP via an active _fx_ complementarity equation
* (else PATH drops the fixed column, leaving the _fx_ row unmatched).
* ============================================
x.lo('1') = -inf;
x.up('1') = +inf;
y.lo('1') = -inf;
y.up('1') = +inf;
y.lo('2') = -inf;
y.up('2') = +inf;

* ============================================
* Equations
* ============================================

* Stationarity: One equation per primal variable (except objvar)
* Complementarity: Equations for inequalities and bounds
* Equality constraints: Original equality constraints

Equations
    stat_area(i)
    stat_x(i)
    stat_y(i)
    comp_maxdist(i,j)
    areadef(i)
    obj2
    x_fx_1
    y_fx_1
    y_fx_2
;

* ============================================
* Equation Definitions
* ============================================

$onMultiR
* Stationarity equations
stat_area(i).. -1 + nu_areadef(i) =E= 0;
stat_x(i).. ((-1) * (0.5 * y(i))) * nu_areadef(i) + (((-1) * (0.5 * ((-1) * y(i)))) * nu_areadef(i+5))$(ord(i) <= card(i) - 5) + (((-1) * (0.5 * ((-1) * y(i)))) * nu_areadef(i-1))$(ord(i) > 1) + nu_x_fx_1$(sameas(i, '1')) + sum(j, (2 * (x(i) - x(j)) * lam_maxdist(i,j))$(ord(i) < ord(j))) + sum(j, (2 * (x(j) - x(i)) * (-1) * lam_maxdist(j,i))$(ord(j) < ord(i) and (not sameas(j, i)))) =E= 0;
stat_y(i).. ((-1) * (0.5 * ((-1) * x(i)))) * nu_areadef(i) + (((-1) * (0.5 * x(i))) * nu_areadef(i+5))$(ord(i) <= card(i) - 5) + (((-1) * (0.5 * x(i))) * nu_areadef(i-1))$(ord(i) > 1) + nu_y_fx_1$(sameas(i, '1')) + nu_y_fx_2$(sameas(i, '2')) + sum(j, (2 * (y(i) - y(j)) * lam_maxdist(i,j))$(ord(i) < ord(j))) + sum(j, (2 * (y(j) - y(i)) * (-1) * lam_maxdist(j,i))$(ord(j) < ord(i) and (not sameas(j, i)))) =E= 0;

* Inequality complementarity equations
comp_maxdist(i,j)$(ord(i) < ord(j)).. ((-1) * (sqr(x(i) - x(j)) + sqr(y(i) - y(j)) - 1)) =G= 0;

* Original equality equations
areadef(i).. area(i) =E= 0.5 * (x(i) * y(i++1) - y(i) * x(i++1));
obj2.. totarea =E= sum(i, area(i));
x_fx_1.. x("1") - 0 =E= 0;
y_fx_1.. y("1") - 0 =E= 0;
y_fx_2.. y("2") - 0 =E= 0;

$offMulti

* ============================================
* Fix inactive variable instances
* ============================================

* Variables whose paired MCP equation is conditioned must be
* fixed for excluded instances to satisfy MCP matching.

lam_maxdist.fx(i,j)$(not (ord(i) < ord(j))) = 0;

* ============================================
* Model MCP Declaration
* ============================================

* Each line pairs an equation with a variable:
*   equation.variable
*
* This defines the complementarity problem:
*   equation ⊥ variable
*
* Meaning: equation = 0 if variable > 0
*          equation ≥ 0 if variable = 0

Model mcp_model /
    stat_area.area,
    stat_x.x,
    stat_y.y,
    comp_maxdist.lam_maxdist,
    areadef.nu_areadef,
    obj2.totarea,
    x_fx_1.nu_x_fx_1,
    y_fx_1.nu_y_fx_1,
    y_fx_2.nu_y_fx_2
/;

* ============================================
* Solve Statement
* ============================================

Solve mcp_model using MCP;

Scalar nlp2mcp_obj_val;
nlp2mcp_obj_val = totarea.l;
Display nlp2mcp_obj_val;